import System.IO.Console;
program AgentsExe;

// HOW A SPECIES ENDED. When the last one is gone it is gone for good -- no respawn, no hidden
// reserve, no quiet re-seed -- and a world that loses its mammoths should be able to say WHICH of
// these it was, in the same breath as saying that it happened.
//
// SEALED, so a fourth way for a species to end cannot be added without every `match` over this being
// told. That matters more here than almost anywhere: the causes arrive one per slice -- eaten out
// and starved are in S1, hunted out arrives with the people in S2, habitat lost with the nations in
// S3 -- and a constant added three slices from now must not land in somebody's `default`.
//
// TWO OF THESE ARE NOT IN THE SPEC, WHICH NAMED THREE, and both were added because a real world
// produced a death the three could not describe. The fauna design says extinction is announced with
// what did it: "hunted out, eaten out, or squeezed out when its habitat was built over".
//
//   `Starved` -- a predator whose prey has been eaten out is neither eaten nor squeezed, and §4 of
//   the same document says in as many words that it starves. The first ten seconds of the real game
//   with predators in it starved 734 animals.
//
//   `DiedOut` -- the last of a species dying of age is not a thing that was DONE to it. A species
//   ends this way when nothing was born to replace it, which is a different sentence from all four
//   of the others and is the one an over-hunted world will most often produce: the killing stops
//   below the breeding threshold, and then it simply runs out.
//
// Without them the answer to "what became of the wolves" would have had to be one of the things that
// did not happen. Recorded in the ledger as S1-6; the spec sentence is corrected with them.
public bundle Agents {
    public namespace Sim {

        public sealed enum Vanished permits
            EatenOut,      // taken by predators, one at a time, until there were none
            Starved,       // a predator with nothing left to catch
            DiedOut,       // the last of them died of age and nothing was born to replace it
            HuntedOut,     // taken by people. S2
            HabitatLost;   // the ground it lived on became something else. S3
    }
}
